  "prefLabel": "Cul-H 204.13 Role of Agency Staff and Complainants",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Cul-H 204.13 Role of Agency Staff and Complainants.\n\n(a) Unless called as witnesses, agency staff shall have no role in any enforcement or disciplinary hearing.\n\n(b) Unless called as a witness, or granted party or intervenor status, a person who initiates an adjudicative proceeding by complaining to the division about the conduct of a person who becomes a party shall have no role in any enforcement or disciplinary hearing.\n\nSource. #10218, eff 10-30-12, EXPIRED: 7-1-18",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/cul-h200.html"
